    "specPath": "specs/052-self-registered-client-tokens/spec.md",
    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "Spec 025 B-7 offers rauthy's dynamic client registration, and B-3 and D-2 make the cell origin in `aud` mandatory. On the pinned rauthy those two cannot both hold for a client that registers itself: rauthy refuses any RFC 8707 `resource` from a dynamic client, and its only other route to an audience is `default_aud`, which only an administrator can set (025 D-12, 037 D-7). Three more defaults stand between a self-registered client and admission: rauthy signs its access tokens EdDSA where the chassis accepts RS256 only, grants it only `openid profile email groups`, and gives it a thirty-minute lifetime above the cell's ceiling; and the packaged cell passes none of rauthy's dynamic client settings at all. This spec makes the packaged cell configure rauthy so a standards-only client (RFC 7591 registration, RFC 8707 resource, PKCE) gets an admissible token, without relaxing the audience check.\n",
    "title": "Self-registered client tokens: a client that registers itself through dynamic registration and asks for this cell with an RFC 8707 resource indicator receives a token the resource server admits, with no administrator call"
  },
